mathjax                    4.1.3  Apache-2.0  https://github.com/mathjax/MathJax
@mathjax/mathjax-tex-font  4.1.3  Apache-2.0 + OFL-1.1  https://github.com/mathjax/MathJax-fonts

Vendored from the npm registry tarballs by Tools/fetch-equation-preview-assets.mjs,
which verifies each tarball against the pinned npm dist.integrity (sha512)
before extracting and records a sha256 per file in manifest.json.
`node Tools/fetch-equation-preview-assets.mjs --check` re-verifies the tree.

Entry point: mathjax/tex-svg-nofont.js — the TeX->SVG combined component
with NO embedded font (loader, startup, core, input/tex, output/svg,
ui/menu).  The mathjax-tex font ships as mathjax-tex-font/svg.js, which
contains all glyph data inline — this package has no dynamic font files, so
rendering never loads anything asynchronously.

The renderer page MUST set
    MathJax.loader.paths.mathjax = <URL of this mathjax/ directory>
    MathJax.loader.paths.fonts   = <same directory>
    MathJax.output.font          = 'mathjax-tex'
before tex-svg-nofont.js executes (inline or via <script src>).  Rationale:

  * output.font — without it the bundle defaults to 'mathjax-newcm' and the
    loader looks for mathjax-newcm-font/svg.js, which is intentionally NOT
    vendored (its upstream NewCM glyph provenance is GUST/GPL-3+FE+DE —
    rejected for this license-sensitive slice).  The lookup then fails
    closed against the local tree; it cannot reach the network because
    paths.fonts is local and the page's CSP/resource policy is restrictive.
  * paths.fonts — upstream default is https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mathjax.
    The bundle derives paths["mathjax-tex"]="[fonts]/mathjax-tex-font" and
    loads "[mathjax-tex]/svg" → mathjax-tex-font/svg.js locally.
  * paths.mathjax — TeX autoload and \require resolve extension files as
    "[mathjax]/input/tex/extensions/<name>.js"; all 41 extension files are
    vendored under input/tex/extensions/, so autoload never leaves the
    directory.  \require accepts alnum names only; unvendored names fail
    closed against the local path.

Font provenance and license: mathjax-tex is the original MathJax TeX font
set (MathJax-authored glyph data, the same font MathJax v2/v3 shipped).
The npm package.json declares Apache-2.0 for the package, while the font's
own legal declaration is SIL OFL 1.1:
  upstream source: @mathjax/mathjax-tex-font@4.1.3 tarball,
    file def/mathjax-tex.ts lines 1547-1550
    (legal: { copyright: 'Copyright (c) 2022, MathJax, Inc.',
              license: SIL_LICENSE, licenseURL: SIL_URL }),
    sha256(bbb6865312e7a6d42d142e641d3075616635c88d75f741adb1ce533ae5255953).
Both notices are honored: the npm-package Apache-2.0 text is mathjax/LICENSE,
and the canonical OFL-1.1 text is mathjax-tex-font/OFL-1.1.txt (sha256
8eea8287e5876b539670cadb82e99f9a7afddec6f6730811be1daf25d2e9bcfd, SPDX
license-list-data).  mathjax-tex-font/package.json is retained as the npm
provenance record.

Coverage: mathjax-tex covers all standard AMS math required by the preview
(fractions, roots, sums/integrals, all listed environments, \mathbb, \mathcal,
\mathfrak, \text, accents, delimiters, extensible arrows).  Some exotic
Unicode ranges that mathjax-newcm supported (e.g. braille, phonetics, PUA)
render as missing glyphs rather than fetching anything — integrators should
route such input to the opt-in exact-TeX path rather than pretend fidelity.

Not vendored: a11y/*, sre/*, input/mml/entities.js — the preview is TeX->SVG
only; assistive-MML/explorer/speech features must stay disabled or those
components would attempt component loads.  ui/safe.js is vendored for an
optional MathJax-side sanitizer (loader.load('ui/safe')).
